# reading-papers: this is a PUBLIC repo, so the rule here is DEFAULT DENY.
# Everything under it is excluded, and only files WE wrote are added back.
#
# Why default-deny rather than listing what to exclude: a deny-list has to be
# updated every time a new kind of file appears. The first attempt at this
# listed paper.pdf and page.html by name, and silently let through 84 PDFs
# (197 MB) sitting in claude-recommendations/ and prof-recommendation/ -
# directories the old blanket rule had been covering. Default-deny cannot
# fail that way: anything new is excluded until someone adds it on purpose.
#
# NOTE: patterns must start at column 0. A leading space makes the pattern
# match a path that literally begins with a space, i.e. nothing.
DOCS/reading-papers/**
# re-include directories so git will descend into them and see the files below
!DOCS/reading-papers/**/
# ---- our own writing, and nothing else ----
!DOCS/reading-papers/sources/**/paper.md
!DOCS/reading-papers/sources/**/meta.yaml
!DOCS/reading-papers/tools/*.py
!DOCS/reading-papers/tools/manifest.yaml
!DOCS/reading-papers/table.md
!DOCS/reading-papers/index.yaml
!DOCS/reading-papers/README.md
!DOCS/reading-papers/FUTURE-BLUEPRINT-REFERENCES.md
# the extracted text layer of the PDFs is the FULL TEXT of IEEE/ACM papers.
# Excluded by the blanket rule above; restated because it is the single worst
# thing that could reach a public repo. Regenerable with tools/pdf_text.py.
DOCS/reading-papers/tools/.cache/**

# downloaded cluster results - large, and they live on Trillium
results-download/

# demo trace index - 37 MB, fetched by demo/fetch_data.sh
demo/data/*.gz
demo/data/sessions/
